1
00:00:00,023 --> 00:00:01,823
in Estonia where I live, the clock changes

2
00:00:01,823 --> 00:00:02,943
twice in a year

3
00:00:02,943 --> 00:00:04,423
on the 29th of March,

4
00:00:04,553 --> 00:00:06,973
the clocks in Tallinn jump from 3 a.m

5
00:00:06,973 --> 00:00:07,843
straight to 4 a.m

6
00:00:07,843 --> 00:00:08,873
so 3:30

7
00:00:09,223 --> 00:00:10,553
that morning never happened

8
00:00:10,633 --> 00:00:12,163
the same way on the 25th

9
00:00:12,383 --> 00:00:12,873
of

10
00:00:13,023 --> 00:00:13,623
October,

11
00:00:14,383 --> 00:00:15,063
the clock

12
00:00:15,223 --> 00:00:16,263
went from 4 a.m

13
00:00:16,263 --> 00:00:17,203
back to 3 a.m

14
00:00:17,203 --> 00:00:18,033
so 3:30

15
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:19,390
happened twice

16
00:00:19,610 --> 00:00:22,250
now imagine our online shop sends a daily

17
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:24,780
sales report at 3:30, Tallinn time

18
00:00:25,070 --> 00:00:26,460
on one day of the year,

19
00:00:26,670 --> 00:00:28,370
that job would not run

20
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:29,950
on another day of the year, it would run

21
00:00:29,950 --> 00:00:30,430
twice

22
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:31,767
so these are things to consider
